{#
    The top navigation: where a reader can go from anywhere.

    Configuration, like the mark and the footer — a theme that read the
    toctree here would put every page of a manual in the bar, which is what
    the rail is for. What belongs up here is the handful of places a site has,
    and only the site knows them:

        <navigation>
            <link href="/frontend" label="Frontend"/>
            <link href="https://example.org" label="Elsewhere" external="true"/>
        </navigation>

    Pills rather than a list, and the active one is a filled block rather than
    a tint — the same rule the rest of the system follows, and one of exactly
    three places the accent appears.
#}
{%- if soul.navigation.links is defined and soul.navigation.links %}
    <nav class="sds-pills" aria-label="Sections">
        {%- for link in soul.navigation.links %}
            {%- set url = link.external ? link.href : renderLink(link.href) %}
            <a class="sds-pill{% if url == '#' %} is-active{% endif %}" href="{{ url }}"
               {%- if link.external %} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"{% endif %}
               {%- if url == '#' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.label }}</a>
        {%- endfor %}
    </nav>
{%- endif -%}
